      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Spondylolisthesis in children and adolescents can present in various ways and have a wide range of treatment options. Children are not \"little adults.\" They require special interview, evaluation, and treatment considerations. This article addresses the characteristics of spondylolisthesis in children and reviews some of the treatment options and related nursing considerations."},
